# Cita del SOFTWARE (el explorador). Para los DATOS se cita el conjunto de cada país con su DOI.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use the data of a country,
  cite that country's ParlaIbero dataset with its DOI as well.
type: software
title: "ParlaIbero Explorer: a browser application for the ParlaIbero corpora of plenary speeches"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained web application that loads the interventions file of a ParlaIbero country
  (Harvard Dataverse) and builds a full-text database in the browser (SQLite with FTS5 compiled to
  WebAssembly) to search, read and analyse the plenary speeches of 16 Ibero-American parliaments.
  Nothing leaves the user's computer.
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues-Silveira
    given-names: Rodrigo
    affiliation: "Instituto de Iberoamérica, Universidad de Salamanca"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6912-7689"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rodrodr/parlaibero-explorer"
url: "https://rodrodr.github.io/parlaibero-explorer/"
keywords:
  - parliamentary speeches
  - legislative debates
  - Latin America
  - Spain
  - Portugal
  - full-text search
  - WebAssembly
references:
  - type: data
    title: "ParlaIbero: Parliamentary Speeches from Latin America, Portugal and Spain"
    authors:
      - name: ParlaIbero
    publisher:
      name: Harvard Dataverse
    url: "https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/parlaibero"
    notes: "Collection. Each country is a dataset with its own DOI, authorship and version."
